{"name":"Blackberry Cordial","hex":"#4f3357","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blackberry","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A fruit-bearing shrub of the aggregate species Rubus fruticosus and some hybrids.","The soft fruit borne by this shrub, formed of a black (when ripe) cluster of drupelets."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To gather or forage for blackberries."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blackberry"},{"term":"cordial","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Hearty; sincere; warm; affectionate.","Radiating warmth and friendliness; genial."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A concentrated non-carbonated soft drink which is diluted with water before drinking.","An individual serving of such a diluted drink."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cordial"}],"entries":[{"title":"Blackberry","blocks":[{"text":"A blackberry is an edible fruit produced by many species in the genus Rubus in the family Rosaceae, hybrids among these species within the subgenus Rubus, and hybrids between the subgenera Rubus and Idaeobatus. The taxonomy of blackberries has historically been confused because of hybridization and apomixis so that species have often been grouped together and called species aggregates."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/78/Ripe%2C_ripening%2C_and_green_blackberries.jpg/330px-Ripe%2C_ripening%2C_and_green_blackberries.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blackberry","wikidata":"Q19842373"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Rubus_fruticosus_Luc_Viatour.JPG/500px-Rubus_fruticosus_Luc_Viatour.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Rubus_fruticosus_Luc_Viatour.JPG/1280px-Rubus_fruticosus_Luc_Viatour.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=pa